{{also|Schreiben}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|schrīben}}, from {{inh|de|goh|scrīban}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*skrīban}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*skrībaną}}, a late borrowing from {{der|de|la|scrībō||write}}, which comes from a word meaning "to scribe, to scrape".

Compare {{cog|nds|schrieven}}, {{cog|nl|schrijven}}, {{cog|en|shrive}} and {{m|en|scribe}}, {{cog|fy|skriuwe}}, {{cog|da|skrive}}, {{cog|sv|skriva}}, {{cog|is|skrifa}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃʁaɪ̯bən/|[ˈʃʁaɪ̯bən]|[-ʃʁaɪ̯bm̩]}}
* {{hyphenation|de|schrei|ben}}
* {{a|South Germany}} {{audio|de|De-schreiben.ogg}}
* {{a|Germany|stressed}} {{audio|de|De-schreiben3.ogg}}
* {{a|Germany|unstressed}} {{audio|de|De-schreiben2.ogg}}
* {{a|Austria}} {{audio|de|De-at-schreiben.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|schreiben<schrieb,geschrieben>}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[write]], to [[write out]] {{gloss|use letters to make words and texts}}
#: {{uxi|de|Sie '''schreibt''' ihren Namen an die Tafel.|She '''writes''' her name on the blackboard.}}
#: {{uxi|de|Er hat einen Artikel '''geschrieben'''.|He’s '''written''' an article.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[spell]] {{gloss|use a particular combination of letters to make a word}}
#: {{uxi|de|Wie '''schreibt''' man das?|How do you '''spell''' that?}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[write]] {{gloss|use handwriting}}
#: {{uxi|de|Sie '''schreibt''' sehr ordentlich.|She '''writes''' very neatly.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[write]] {{gloss|produce texts, work as an author}}
#: {{uxi|de|Er '''schreibt''' sehr anschaulich.|He '''writes''' very vividly.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|usually with {{m|de|man}} or {{m|de|wir}}}} to be some [[year]] or [[date]]
#: {{uxi|de|Man '''schrieb''' das Jahr 1874, als...|It was the year 1874 when...|lit=One '''wrote''' the year 1874 when...}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|or|intransitive|+ [[dative]]}} to [[write]], to [[text]] {{gloss|send written information, communication}}
#: {{uxi|de|Er hat mir eine Mail '''geschrieben'''.|He’s '''written''' me an e-mail.}}
#: {{uxi|de|Der verwundete Soldat '''schrieb''' seiner Frau.|The wounded soldier '''wrote''' to his wife.}}
#: {{uxi|de|Ich '''schreibe''' dir, wenn ich fast da bin.|I’ll '''text''' you when I’m almost there.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|or|intransitive|+ [[reflexive]] [[dative]]}} to [[write]] to [[each other]] {{gloss|exchange correspondance}}
#: {{uxi|de|Sie '''schreiben''' sich immer Postkarten.|They always '''write''' each other postcards.}}
#: {{uxi|de|Wir '''schreiben''' uns regelmäßig.|We '''write''' to each other on a regular basis.}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to be [[spell]]ed/spelt; {{ngd|of a word or a person's name}}
#: {{uxi|de|Wie '''schreibt''' sich das?|How do you spell that?|lit=How does that '''spell''' itself?}}
#: {{uxi|de|Wie '''schreiben''' Sie sich?|How is your name spelt?|lit=How do you '''spell''' yourself?}}

